=== Prompt for SKY-004-A (attempt 1) ===
Implement user story SKY-004-A: Server skeleton: /health, GET /, API-key middleware, error handling, and package.json scripts

## Story Description
Create the Express server skeleton in src/server.ts with the module-guard pattern, the /health and GET / routes, the RAPIDAPI_KEY absence middleware (503 short-circuit), the global error handler (500), and the package.json 'start'/'build' scripts. This slice has no runtime dependency on SKY-002 and can be implemented and merged in parallel with it. supertest and @types/supertest must be installed. A minimal test file (at least 4 tests) covering /health, GET /, 503 gating, and the module-guard must pass.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports a named `app` (Express instance) separately from the `listen()` call so supertest can import it without binding a port
- The `listen()` call in src/server.ts is guarded using the pattern matching the tsup output format (CJS: `require.main === module`; ESM: `import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href`) so `vitest run` never binds a port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type application/json and body matching { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> }
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 regardless of whether RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is set or absent
- GET / returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type matching text/html and body equal to the contents of src/public/index.html
- src/public/index.html exists and contains valid HTML with at minimum a non-empty file with an <html> root element
- When RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent at server initialisation, a single middleware short-circuits GET /search and GET /cheapest with HTTP 503 Content-Type application/json body { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; GET /health and GET / are unaffected
- When SkyscannerClient throws during a request, the server returns HTTP 500 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string } and does not crash or emit an unhandled promise rejection
- package.json contains a 'start' script with value 'node dist/server.js'
- package.json contains a 'build' script that produces dist/server.js such that `npm run build && npm run start` starts the server and GET /health returns HTTP 200
- supertest and @types/supertest are listed in package.json devDependencies
- `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0 with no type errors
- `vitest run` exits 0 with all tests passing (minimum 4 tests covering /health, GET /, 503 gating, and module-guard isolation)

